Z||000000||Shiner||11-30-1999||05:23 PM||||I am getting ready to mount the spoiler I got from someone off this message board.  Now, I belive he said that the spoiler was from an '86 notchback.  The car it's being mounted to is an '87 GT.  I noticed that the spacing between the holes on the decklid is longer than the spacing between the bolts on the mounts.  Drilling a couple new holes is no big deal here.  I just want to know; should I put the REAR spoiler bolts in the REAR bolt holes on the decklid, and drill new fronts?  Or should I line up the fronts and drill new rears?  I just want it to be in the stock location.  Thanks guys.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Shiner||12-01-1999||12:55 AM||||Ogre? Anybody?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wolfhound||12-01-1999||04:15 AM||||Shiner, I have an 87 GT with factory spoiler. I,ll post an exact measurement fom the back of the rear deck to the rear of the spoiler mount first thing in the morning.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shiner||12-01-1999||04:38 AM||||Thanks alot Wolf, that would be alot of help  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000004||Wolfhound||12-01-1999||07:37 AM||||Shiner, It,s 5 and 1/8 inches from the rear of the pedestal to the rear of the deck lid.<BR>Coy||||reg||1
Z||000005||Sage||12-01-1999||08:19 AM||||Check on the bottom of the spoiler( if it is a factory spoiler) and see if there are two places for the mounting studs to screw in.  If there are see if one set lines up with the holes you have in your deck.  IF there are, and IF they do, you just need to unscrew the stud that doesn't line up and put into the hole that will!  Hope this makes sense to you, if you are not talking about a factory spoiler, then this is probably all mute anyway, but I went thru this with a spoiler and they have two different sets of mounting holes in the bottom of the uprights, at least the one I had did!  Moving the studs is much simpler,faster, and easier than drilling holes in your deck lid.  Let us know how you make out.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
